<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33127" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτῡφόω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>delude, deceive</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ πλήθη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>puff up</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑαυτόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					2.569
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				215
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				16.21.12
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>vanish into smoke</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς καπνὸν ἐκτυφοῦται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					1.68.2
				</span></i>
			; but perh. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτύφεται</span> shd.
			be read; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτύφονται</span> is 
				v.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τυφοῦνται</span>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.68.5
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
